  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "For an array AAA of length NNN and a non-negative integer mmm, we define the function fm(A)f_m(A)fm​(A) as\n\nfm(A)=∑i=1NAi⋅imf_m(A) = \\sum_{i=1}^N A_i \\cdot i^mfm​(A)=i=1∑N​Ai​⋅imYou are given two integers NNN and CCC.\n\nA sequence AAA of non-negative integers of length KKK is said to be good if it satisfies the following four conditions:\n\n\n1≤K≤N1 \\leq K \\leq N1≤K≤N\n0≤A1≤A2≤A3≤…≤AK0 \\le A_1 \\leq A_2\\leq A_3 \\leq \\ldots \\leq A_K0≤A1​≤A2​≤A3​≤…≤AK​\nf0(A)=Nf_0(A) = Nf0​(A)=N\nf1(A)=Cf_1(A) = Cf1​(A)=C\nIf there is no sequence that is good, print −1-1−1.\n\nOtherwise, let MMM denote the minimum possible value of f2(A)f_2(A)f2​(A) across all good sequences.\n\nCompute MMM, and also construct any good sequence AAA for which f2(A)=Mf_2(A) = Mf2​(A)=M.\n\nIf there are multiple possible good sequences for which f2(A)=Mf_2(A) = Mf2​(A)=M, you may find any of them.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of a single line of input, which contains two space-separated integers NNN and CCC.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case:\n\n\n\nIf there is no sequence that satisfies the conditions, print a single line containing the integer −1-1−1.\nIf a good sequence exists,\n\nOn the first line, print a single integer — the minimum possible value of f2(A)f_2(A)f2​(A) across all good sequences.\nOn the second line, print the length of the sequence AAA you will construct - a single integer KKK.\nOn the third line, print KKK space-separated integers A1,A2,…,AKA_1,A_2,\\ldots,A_KA1​,A2​,…,AK​, denoting the sequence you constructed.\n\n\n\nIf there are multiple valid sequences, you may print any of them.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤2⋅1051 \\leq T \\leq 2\\cdot 10^51≤T≤2⋅105",
      "1≤N≤1061 \\leq N \\leq 10^61≤N≤106",
      "1≤C≤10181 \\leq C \\leq 10^{18}1≤C≤1018",
      "The sum of NNN across all tests won't exceed 10610^{6}106."
    ],
